1
00:00:13,888 --> 00:00:16,933
OUR STICKY LOVE

2
00:00:25,734 --> 00:00:26,568
Chairman, sir.

3
00:00:27,569 --> 00:00:29,654
Prosecutor Go isn't on the cargo ship.

4
00:00:36,327 --> 00:00:37,787
Baek Sang-gil!

5
00:01:09,069 --> 00:01:10,987
So we meet like this.

6
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:13,907
I used to call you Coach.

7
00:01:15,283 --> 00:01:16,951
But what should I call you now?

8
00:01:18,286 --> 00:01:20,914
There isn't really a way
for an abandoned disciple

9
00:01:21,414 --> 00:01:22,874
to address their master.

10
00:01:25,001 --> 00:01:26,835
1991 NATIONAL BOXING TEAM
FINAL SELECTION

11
00:01:26,836 --> 00:01:28,837
LIGHT WELTERWEIGHT MATCHUP

12
00:01:28,838 --> 00:01:30,590
BAEK SANG-GIL
VS LEE JUNG-GU

13
00:01:32,217 --> 00:01:34,968
Baek Sang-gil is in great form today.

14
00:01:34,969 --> 00:01:38,389
At this rate, Baek Sang-gil's gold medal
is almost guaranteed.

15
00:01:41,059 --> 00:01:41,893
No holding.

16
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:47,232
Baek Sang-gil is really going for it.

17
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:55,740
No holding. Break!

18
00:02:00,328 --> 00:02:01,454
Stop!

19
00:02:04,749 --> 00:02:05,833
What's going on here?

20
00:02:05,834 --> 00:02:06,959
Blue corner.

21
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:08,335
You forfeit. It's over.

22
00:02:08,336 --> 00:02:12,047
Baek Sang-gil's coach
just threw in the towel.

23
00:02:12,048 --> 00:02:15,759
It's not uncommon for a coach
to throw in the towel

24
00:02:15,760 --> 00:02:17,928
to protect their fighter at risk.

25
00:02:17,929 --> 00:02:20,639
But, in this case,
Baek Sang-gil had the upper hand.

26
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:22,850
- Exactly.
- It's a little baffling.

27
00:02:22,851 --> 00:02:25,645
Baek Sang-gil also looks
very confused right now.

28
00:02:27,856 --> 00:02:28,940
Coach!

29
00:02:30,567 --> 00:02:31,943
What the heck did you…

30
00:02:33,319 --> 00:02:34,320
Take them off.

31
00:02:41,327 --> 00:02:43,788
Thought I wouldn't hear
the difference in your gloves?

32
00:02:45,748 --> 00:02:49,751
I had it in the bag. I was so close
to becoming a national athlete.

33
00:02:49,752 --> 00:02:53,297
You think you can become
a national athlete with such dirty fists?

34
00:02:53,298 --> 00:02:55,800
Wouldn't it be good for you
if I make the national team?

35
00:02:57,886 --> 00:03:00,971
Taking you in as my disciple,
even for a short time,

36
00:03:00,972 --> 00:03:03,265
will have been
the most shameful thing in my life.

37
00:03:03,266 --> 00:03:06,019
- Coach!
- From this moment on, I'm not your coach.

38
00:03:06,811 --> 00:03:09,189
I never taught you
to use your fists to harm others.

39
00:03:14,652 --> 00:03:15,945
Fuck this!

40
00:03:18,406 --> 00:03:22,076
<i>I cherish Jang Tae-ha as if he were made
from my own rib.</i>

41
00:03:22,744 --> 00:03:25,287
<i>And soon, not only me</i>

42
00:03:25,288 --> 00:03:30,335
<i>but all of Korea will come to cherish him
as a great athlete.</i>

43
00:03:45,516 --> 00:03:49,103
Your disciple who wound up on
the same path as me, whom you despised.

44
00:03:50,188 --> 00:03:52,731
I'm sure it wasn't easy to take him back.

45
00:03:52,732 --> 00:03:55,777
I'm truly sorry
things turned out this way.

46
00:03:56,778 --> 00:03:57,695
You know what?

47
00:04:10,875 --> 00:04:13,795
The thrill of throwing punches
with your life on the line

48
00:04:14,587 --> 00:04:18,883
makes those pretty little jabs in the ring
pale in comparison.

49
00:04:23,179 --> 00:04:25,556
Even after 30 years,

50
00:04:27,433 --> 00:04:30,228
you haven't changed one bit,
Baek Sang-gil.

51
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:33,982
Do you think you corrupted

52
00:04:34,941 --> 00:04:36,401
someone I care about?

53
00:04:38,152 --> 00:04:39,070
You didn't.

54
00:04:39,946 --> 00:04:40,947
Tae-ha

55
00:04:41,614 --> 00:04:43,199
has never been corrupted.

56
00:04:44,826 --> 00:04:48,663
Even now, you're trying
to kill innocent folks for your own greed.

57
00:04:49,163 --> 00:04:51,833
But Tae-ha did all this
to save someone's life.

58
00:04:55,044 --> 00:04:56,254
So

59
00:04:57,171 --> 00:04:58,965
you've got nothing to be proud of.

60
00:05:07,974 --> 00:05:12,061
I reported a car explosion,
so the police will be here soon.

61
00:05:12,854 --> 00:05:15,148
If you have the guts,
stay and see what happens.

62
00:05:52,310 --> 00:05:53,436
Tae-ha.

63
00:05:54,979 --> 00:05:55,855
Are you okay?

64
00:05:58,274 --> 00:05:59,317
Can you get up?

65
00:05:59,817 --> 00:06:00,818
Try to get up.

66
00:06:13,414 --> 00:06:16,042
I told you not to get involved.

67
00:06:16,542 --> 00:06:18,210
Why did you come?

68
00:06:18,211 --> 00:06:23,006
Even if you had Gang-rok, the gas cans,
and were ready to call the police,

69
00:06:23,007 --> 00:06:26,135
what if something went wrong?
How could you go at him like that?

70
00:06:27,845 --> 00:06:30,932
Still… Go Eun-sae got away.

71
00:06:33,768 --> 00:06:34,685
Safely.

72
00:06:36,104 --> 00:06:37,772
She got away safely.

73
00:06:44,278 --> 00:06:46,864
No, Jang Tae-ha!

74
00:07:02,338 --> 00:07:03,464
Tae-ha.

75
00:07:04,173 --> 00:07:05,173
Tae-ha!

76
00:07:05,174 --> 00:07:07,343
Stay with me. Tae-ha!

77
00:07:07,927 --> 00:07:09,929
Hey, stay with me! Tae-ha!

78
00:07:22,024 --> 00:07:23,942
- Let go.
- I won't. We have to go.

79
00:07:23,943 --> 00:07:25,485
I have to go now!

80
00:07:25,486 --> 00:07:26,736
If you do, you'll die.

81
00:07:26,737 --> 00:07:28,281
I said let go of me!

82
00:07:29,073 --> 00:07:30,157
Step on their foot,

83
00:07:30,158 --> 00:07:31,199
trip them up,

84
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:32,076
and run away.

85
00:07:44,422 --> 00:07:45,715
Ms. Go Eun-sae!

86
00:07:46,507 --> 00:07:47,341
Damn it.

87
00:08:12,867 --> 00:08:14,660
I'M DONE
LEAVE AT THE COAST GUARD SIREN

88
00:08:19,832 --> 00:08:21,250
What the… Eun-sae?

89
00:08:24,086 --> 00:08:25,254
Kaito?

90
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:27,524
Just don't disappear without a word.
Just stay out of danger.

91
00:09:27,525 --> 00:09:28,651
Just…

92
00:09:30,403 --> 00:09:32,071
<i>Just stay safe.</i>

93
00:10:43,851 --> 00:10:44,685
Park Hyo-jin.

94
00:10:48,731 --> 00:10:49,982
You bitch.

95
00:11:03,579 --> 00:11:04,789
Is it back?

96
00:11:05,414 --> 00:11:06,415
Your memory?

97
00:11:09,126 --> 00:11:10,127
Yeah,

98
00:11:11,087 --> 00:11:12,505
you bitch.

99
00:11:32,817 --> 00:11:34,443
What's with the bag of taffy?

100
00:11:35,194 --> 00:11:37,779
All I knew was
that you were in some taffy village,

101
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:39,615
so what else could I do?

102
00:11:40,408 --> 00:11:44,912
You deleted your Instagram account,
and I lost your new phone number.

103
00:11:46,706 --> 00:11:49,040
Why bother searching for a bitch
you hate so much?

104
00:11:49,041 --> 00:11:52,461
If you got your revenge,
you should've moved on for good.

105
00:11:53,587 --> 00:11:55,589
You don't even have the guts to do that.

106
00:11:59,051 --> 00:12:00,761
It all came back to me.

107
00:12:19,780 --> 00:12:21,365
Hey, switch shoes with me.

108
00:12:24,493 --> 00:12:25,619
Hey.

109
00:12:52,313 --> 00:12:53,689
The hurt kept piling up,

110
00:12:54,398 --> 00:12:57,151
and I'd forgotten about
all the good times we'd shared.

111
00:12:57,651 --> 00:13:00,029
But after I got my revenge on you,

112
00:13:01,071 --> 00:13:03,783
all the hurt disappeared,
and I could see it again.

113
00:13:05,159 --> 00:13:06,619
The good times we had.

114
00:13:08,370 --> 00:13:11,207
And the sort of friend you used to be.

115
00:13:13,876 --> 00:13:14,876
I'm sorry.

116
00:13:14,877 --> 00:13:16,712
I lived my life wrong.

117
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:19,757
I'm really sorry.

118
00:13:20,257 --> 00:13:21,467
It's okay.

119
00:13:22,802 --> 00:13:24,219
I'm sorry for everything.

120
00:13:24,220 --> 00:13:25,970
I'm more sorry.

121
00:13:25,971 --> 00:13:29,016
No. I'm even more sorry.

122
00:13:38,567 --> 00:13:40,652
Eun-sae, drink this while it's warm.

123
00:13:40,653 --> 00:13:41,904
Thanks.

124
00:13:48,285 --> 00:13:49,787
Where were you, really?

125
00:13:51,831 --> 00:13:52,665
Gujin.

126
00:13:53,541 --> 00:13:56,585
Gujin? Right, Gujin.

127
00:13:57,253 --> 00:13:59,463
So there's a taffy village there too.

128
00:14:00,005 --> 00:14:04,677
And who was the person who took you in?

129
00:14:11,392 --> 00:14:15,604
He was… someone that I knew.

130
00:14:16,981 --> 00:14:18,899
What's your name?

131
00:14:19,733 --> 00:14:21,526
Jang Tae-ha.

132
00:14:21,527 --> 00:14:23,862
<i>We had met before,</i>

133
00:14:23,863 --> 00:14:26,865
and he was someone
who left me with a good memory.

134
00:14:26,866 --> 00:14:28,992
But I like this one the most.

135
00:14:28,993 --> 00:14:30,702
I met my first love here.

136
00:14:30,703 --> 00:14:31,953
It was nice meeting you,

137
00:14:31,954 --> 00:14:33,706
Mr. Future Gold Medalist.

138
00:14:35,165 --> 00:14:36,374
<i>And it turned out</i>

139
00:14:36,375 --> 00:14:39,295
that we'd first crossed paths
a very long time ago.

140
00:14:46,218 --> 00:14:49,178
MIRAE EDEN COMPANY
ORGANIZATIONAL CHART

141
00:14:49,179 --> 00:14:50,889
JANG TAE-HA
DIRECTOR

142
00:14:50,890 --> 00:14:53,267
I'm sorry that I was

143
00:14:54,226 --> 00:14:55,268
a gangster.

144
00:14:55,269 --> 00:14:57,729
<i>He was an unfortunate person</i>

145
00:14:57,730 --> 00:14:59,982
who lived a life he never wanted.

146
00:15:00,482 --> 00:15:01,317
<i>It's me.</i>

147
00:15:01,817 --> 00:15:03,234
Jang Tae-ha.

148
00:15:03,235 --> 00:15:04,570
Your boyfriend.

149
00:15:05,905 --> 00:15:07,322
We met in the mountains.

150
00:15:07,323 --> 00:15:10,366
Our dog isn't in the yard.

151
00:15:10,367 --> 00:15:12,745
I'll hurry and go find her.

152
00:15:15,873 --> 00:15:18,416
He even put on a clumsy act.

153
00:15:18,417 --> 00:15:20,085
Don't take it too hard.

154
00:15:20,586 --> 00:15:22,671
If you keep living…

155
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:29,261
everything passes.

156
00:15:47,363 --> 00:15:49,281
He's the one who saved me.

157
00:15:52,201 --> 00:15:53,535
Eun-sae.

158
00:15:56,580 --> 00:16:01,085
He risked his life to save me
until the very end.

159
00:16:13,597 --> 00:16:14,765
What was that?

160
00:16:17,142 --> 00:16:20,103
You mean Prosecutor Go
didn't get on the boat?

161
00:16:20,104 --> 00:16:22,606
Then where is Eun-sae right now?

162
00:16:24,525 --> 00:16:25,359
I don't know.

163
00:16:26,360 --> 00:16:30,114
The last thing I saw
was her riding off on my motorcycle.

164
00:16:30,698 --> 00:16:33,242
- Good heavens.
- Goodness, what do we do?

165
00:16:33,826 --> 00:16:35,493
Tae-ha will freak if he finds out.

166
00:16:35,494 --> 00:16:38,830
But even if he does find out,
there's no way for us to find her.

167
00:16:38,831 --> 00:16:41,333
She turned her phone off,
and we can't just…

168
00:16:43,877 --> 00:16:46,422
ask the police for help either.

169
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:50,342
Goodness. What are we gonna do?

170
00:16:58,350 --> 00:17:00,561
Let's not tell Tae-ha for now.

171
00:17:01,437 --> 00:17:03,813
If that punk finds out
she didn't get on the boat,

172
00:17:03,814 --> 00:17:08,109
he'll leave this place in a flash
and scour the entire country for her.

173
00:17:08,110 --> 00:17:10,361
- Yeah.
- Yes, I agree with you.

174
00:17:10,362 --> 00:17:13,365
Instead, I'll look into the facilities
across the country.

175
00:17:14,033 --> 00:17:16,118
Yeah, okay.

176
00:17:27,087 --> 00:17:28,213
Thank goodness.

177
00:17:29,298 --> 00:17:31,967
I'm so glad you had him.

178
00:17:35,262 --> 00:17:38,557
There's only one thing I can do
for Jang Tae-ha.

179
00:17:39,099 --> 00:17:40,726
I need to catch Baek Sang-gil.

180
00:17:41,810 --> 00:17:45,188
- You're going back to work?
- No, I need to see how things go first.

181
00:17:45,189 --> 00:17:47,065
If they put me on long-term leave,

182
00:17:47,066 --> 00:17:49,817
Baek Sang-gil must have people
in the Prosecutor's Office.

183
00:17:49,818 --> 00:17:53,029
Baek Sang-gil tortured me
to find out where my watch was.

184
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:55,324
<i>And in the end, he found it. I saw it.</i>

185
00:17:56,492 --> 00:17:58,576
<i>But even after finding it,
he didn't kill me.</i>

186
00:17:58,577 --> 00:17:59,702
<i>That means</i>

187
00:17:59,703 --> 00:18:01,788
he knows about my plan B.

188
00:18:01,789 --> 00:18:03,831
And the only person who knows about that

189
00:18:03,832 --> 00:18:05,292
is Chi-hyeon.

190
00:18:06,794 --> 00:18:10,047
<i>Actually, when I mentioned
that I was going to report you missing…</i>

191
00:18:10,547 --> 00:18:11,547
She's not missing.

192
00:18:11,548 --> 00:18:14,175
…Chi-hyeon told me not to,
saying you weren't missing.

193
00:18:14,176 --> 00:18:17,137
But something felt off about it.

194
00:18:17,930 --> 00:18:19,472
Does that mean he's also…

195
00:18:19,473 --> 00:18:21,475
He's likely to be one of them.

196
00:18:24,686 --> 00:18:26,563
How could he…

197
00:18:28,315 --> 00:18:29,942
Then what was plan B?

198
00:18:32,236 --> 00:18:33,070
My sneakers.

199
00:18:44,164 --> 00:18:47,917
<i>My sneakers were set to instantly upload
whatever they filmed to my cloud drive.</i>

200
00:18:47,918 --> 00:18:51,420
But when I tried to access the drive
earlier from my phone, I couldn't.

201
00:18:51,421 --> 00:18:53,589
I think they hacked my account too.

202
00:18:53,590 --> 00:18:54,883
Then what do we do?

203
00:18:55,384 --> 00:18:56,592
There is a way.

204
00:18:56,593 --> 00:19:00,930
I had the cameras in my watch and sneakers
synced to my laptop.

205
00:19:00,931 --> 00:19:04,559
So the footage should be saved
on my laptop at home.

206
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:05,394
But

207
00:19:05,978 --> 00:19:07,895
I'm scared to go home right now.

208
00:19:07,896 --> 00:19:10,858
In case Baek Sang-gil's people
might have done something to it?

209
00:19:11,608 --> 00:19:12,442
Yeah.

210
00:19:16,530 --> 00:19:18,073
So, I was wondering…

211
00:19:25,455 --> 00:19:27,957
- How did it go?
- There were no suspicious vehicles.

212
00:19:27,958 --> 00:19:31,044
And there were no bugs or cameras
around your home either.

213
00:19:31,545 --> 00:19:34,923
But there were signs that someone
had tampered with the door lock.

214
00:19:35,424 --> 00:19:36,508
- Sorry?
- Sorry?

215
00:19:37,009 --> 00:19:39,051
We did a thorough check of the place.

216
00:19:39,052 --> 00:19:40,679
It's safe, so you can go in.

217
00:19:41,513 --> 00:19:42,556
Okay, thank you.

218
00:20:12,753 --> 00:20:14,129
What? Your laptop.

219
00:20:16,173 --> 00:20:18,799
Your laptop is gone.

220
00:20:18,800 --> 00:20:21,303
Those bastards must have taken
your laptop too.

221
00:20:22,012 --> 00:20:25,681
Of course.
Baek Sang-gil is a meticulous bastard.

222
00:20:25,682 --> 00:20:26,682
So what now?

223
00:20:26,683 --> 00:20:28,393
Is it saved anywhere else?

224
00:20:30,312 --> 00:20:33,148
It's not. The memory chip in the sneakers
is the last place.

225
00:20:33,774 --> 00:20:34,691
Where are they?

226
00:20:36,526 --> 00:20:38,402
They found no viable fingerprints

227
00:20:38,403 --> 00:20:42,366
on the clothes and shoes you were wearing
when you were found.

228
00:20:43,450 --> 00:20:47,536
Why did I wear a suit with sneakers
instead of dress shoes that day?

229
00:20:47,537 --> 00:20:48,622
So unstylish.

230
00:20:53,585 --> 00:20:54,919
In Taffy Village.

231
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:57,713
That's great. Then let's ask
that Jang Tae-ha guy for help.

232
00:20:57,714 --> 00:20:59,715
And tell him you got your memory back.

233
00:20:59,716 --> 00:21:03,594
We can't do that. If he finds out
my memory's back, he won't just stand by.

234
00:21:03,595 --> 00:21:07,181
He'll definitely try to send me somewhere
or try to protect me.

235
00:21:07,182 --> 00:21:08,725
He'd disrupt the investigation.

236
00:21:10,394 --> 00:21:12,813
I don't want to put him in more danger
because of me.

237
00:21:14,648 --> 00:21:15,732
Then what will you do?

238
00:21:28,829 --> 00:21:29,705
Chairman.

239
00:21:30,330 --> 00:21:32,249
I think Prosecutor Go is in Korea.

240
00:21:33,583 --> 00:21:34,500
What?

241
00:21:34,501 --> 00:21:38,129
I confirmed that no ships left the port
overnight except that cargo ship.

242
00:21:38,130 --> 00:21:42,259
And some of our men saw her
leaving the port on a motorcycle.

243
00:22:07,367 --> 00:22:10,286
Why did you come
when Prosecutor Go isn't even here?

244
00:22:10,287 --> 00:22:14,541
You had the nerve to hide Prosecutor Go
and thought I'd just sit still?

245
00:22:17,002 --> 00:22:19,046
You must be upset
about your dear disciple,

246
00:22:20,213 --> 00:22:24,343
but I always make sure to repay my debts,
favors, and grudges.

247
00:22:26,261 --> 00:22:30,349
Even you praised my tenacity
when I was a boxer, did you not?

248
00:22:39,816 --> 00:22:43,737
If you're going to play the "former coach"
and give me some half-baked advice…

249
00:22:49,826 --> 00:22:50,660
Can't you just

250
00:22:52,120 --> 00:22:53,372
let Tae-ha go now?

251
00:22:55,415 --> 00:22:57,125
Prosecutor Go has lost her memory,

252
00:22:58,168 --> 00:22:59,961
so she can't do you any harm.

253
00:23:02,547 --> 00:23:04,466
If it's me you hate,

254
00:23:05,717 --> 00:23:07,135
then do whatever you want

255
00:23:08,678 --> 00:23:09,513
to me.

256
00:23:13,016 --> 00:23:14,267
Let Tae-ha go.

257
00:23:15,811 --> 00:23:16,686
Let him go.

258
00:23:17,312 --> 00:23:20,107
That poor boy has never lived for himself
his entire life.

259
00:23:21,608 --> 00:23:22,567
Please.

260
00:23:25,862 --> 00:23:26,822
Just leave him…

261
00:23:28,698 --> 00:23:29,699
alone now.

262
00:23:36,581 --> 00:23:37,457
I'm…

263
00:23:39,918 --> 00:23:40,752
I'm…

264
00:23:43,088 --> 00:23:44,256
begging you.

265
00:24:14,202 --> 00:24:15,244
KAITO

266
00:24:15,245 --> 00:24:17,581
I told you,
I spoke with Kaito on the phone.

267
00:24:18,165 --> 00:24:20,459
He said the boat departed safely.

268
00:24:20,959 --> 00:24:24,087
But… I still haven't heard from him, so…

269
00:24:25,255 --> 00:24:26,589
No news is good news.

270
00:24:26,590 --> 00:24:29,550
He'll call when everything's settled.

271
00:24:29,551 --> 00:24:31,761
Get some rest. That's it.

272
00:24:36,308 --> 00:24:37,142
You're up?

273
00:24:38,143 --> 00:24:41,271
- What took you so long at the store?
- Did you stop by somewhere?

274
00:24:41,855 --> 00:24:42,689
Yeah, the bathroom.

275
00:24:45,484 --> 00:24:48,777
Hey, don't worry about others
going to the bathroom.

276
00:24:48,778 --> 00:24:50,489
Worry about yourself.

277
00:24:51,281 --> 00:24:54,409
You're a healthy young man,
not an old man.

278
00:24:55,035 --> 00:24:56,870
What are you doing in a hospital bed?

279
00:24:57,996 --> 00:25:00,414
That's why I'm going home now.

280
00:25:00,415 --> 00:25:02,417
- Goodness.
- Already?

281
00:25:03,710 --> 00:25:06,129
Hey, I didn't mean it like that.

282
00:25:06,922 --> 00:25:10,424
I'm really fine.
There's nothing to do here anyway.

283
00:25:10,425 --> 00:25:12,511
You should recover more…

284
00:25:13,345 --> 00:25:15,346
Stay a bit longer.

285
00:25:15,347 --> 00:25:16,765
- No, I…
- I'm fine.

286
00:25:18,099 --> 00:25:19,559
That's not what I meant.

287
00:25:20,060 --> 00:25:21,393
- Watch your step.
- Careful.

288
00:25:21,394 --> 00:25:23,145
I'll go check Tae-ha's room.

289
00:25:23,146 --> 00:25:26,398
I said stay a bit longer.
Why were you in such a rush to leave?

290
00:25:26,399 --> 00:25:28,109
Should he lie down?

291
00:25:28,902 --> 00:25:30,487
- Hold on.
- Are you okay?

292
00:25:34,491 --> 00:25:36,576
- Grandma.
- Ma'am, you're here?

293
00:25:38,245 --> 00:25:40,829
- Ma'am.
- Ma'am, please.

294
00:25:40,830 --> 00:25:43,750
Tae-ha's condition right now is…

295
00:25:44,251 --> 00:25:45,335
Ma'am, please.

296
00:25:46,211 --> 00:25:52,509
How much more of an inconsiderate
grandmother do you want me to be?

297
00:25:54,010 --> 00:25:56,388
I heard you didn't go because of me.

298
00:25:57,722 --> 00:25:59,557
You like her so much,

299
00:25:59,558 --> 00:26:03,103
but you didn't go
because of my illness again.

300
00:26:04,771 --> 00:26:07,524
How do you expect me to live?

301
00:26:08,525 --> 00:26:11,194
This grandmother,
who held back her grandson twice…

302
00:26:11,820 --> 00:26:14,990
How can I continue to live
with this shame?

303
00:26:18,910 --> 00:26:22,372
And you? How are you going to live?

304
00:26:22,998 --> 00:26:26,126
You let the girl you love
more than your own life go off on her own.

305
00:26:26,626 --> 00:26:29,004
How are you going to live?

306
00:26:35,719 --> 00:26:36,886
Grandma.

307
00:26:38,388 --> 00:26:40,181
It's okay, Grandma.

308
00:26:41,725 --> 00:26:43,643
I can live just fine

309
00:26:45,020 --> 00:26:46,646
even without her.

310
00:26:50,525 --> 00:26:52,652
I'll live just fine.

311
00:26:55,071 --> 00:26:56,530
My poor baby. My baby.

312
00:26:56,531 --> 00:26:59,492
What am I going to do, my baby?

313
00:27:07,709 --> 00:27:09,794
Will you really be okay alone?

314
00:27:10,462 --> 00:27:12,212
Don't worry and go to work.

315
00:27:12,213 --> 00:27:16,133
The security company confirmed it's safe,
and Baek Sang-gil thinks I went to Japan.

316
00:27:16,134 --> 00:27:18,928
So it's actually safer here right now.

317
00:27:20,805 --> 00:27:24,059
Okay. Call me right away
if anything happens.

318
00:27:24,643 --> 00:27:25,477
Okay.

319
00:27:29,105 --> 00:27:30,398
Thank you, Hyo-jin.

320
00:27:31,107 --> 00:27:32,108
Don't be silly.

321
00:27:35,278 --> 00:27:36,528
Don't come out barefoot.

322
00:27:36,529 --> 00:27:37,614
It's okay.

323
00:27:40,033 --> 00:27:41,075
Go inside.

324
00:27:41,076 --> 00:27:43,036
- Okay.
- See you!

325
00:27:55,215 --> 00:27:58,884
They say you don't know when someone
comes, but you know when they leave.

326
00:27:58,885 --> 00:28:01,762
The entire village has gone so quiet

327
00:28:01,763 --> 00:28:05,308
all because Eun-sae has gone.

328
00:28:06,601 --> 00:28:09,479
I wonder if she has arrived safely
in Japan yet.

329
00:28:11,523 --> 00:28:14,067
Stop it, you two.

330
00:28:14,859 --> 00:28:17,487
Why are you thinking about someone
who's gone?

331
00:28:20,865 --> 00:28:26,705
<i>Have you already forgotten me?</i>

332
00:28:28,415 --> 00:28:30,332
<i>Leaving only longing behind…</i>

333
00:28:30,333 --> 00:28:32,376
Light pink roses.

334
00:28:32,377 --> 00:28:35,171
<i>Have you really forgotten me?</i>

335
00:28:35,672 --> 00:28:36,965
They're so pretty.

336
00:28:37,465 --> 00:28:39,008
They were her favorite.

337
00:28:44,597 --> 00:28:47,809
We had so much fun at karaoke.

338
00:28:55,483 --> 00:28:58,737
And she fought like a trooper.

339
00:29:00,405 --> 00:29:03,658
It's no good if it won't work!
Then I guess we should call it a day.

340
00:29:04,159 --> 00:29:07,035
It was such a comfort,
having that feisty hen in my corner.

341
00:29:07,036 --> 00:29:11,708
<i>Oh, what am I to do when I miss you so?</i>

342
00:29:13,376 --> 00:29:18,631
<i>My longing for you only grows</i>

343
00:29:33,354 --> 00:29:34,856
BREAKFAST, LUNCH, DINNER

344
00:30:03,092 --> 00:30:06,888
Easy. Wait, the cushions.

345
00:30:08,348 --> 00:30:10,224
You can go now. I'm fine.

346
00:30:10,225 --> 00:30:11,642
No, it's okay.

347
00:30:11,643 --> 00:30:13,101
I should be here to help you.

348
00:30:13,102 --> 00:30:16,439
You're not well, so it must be hard
for you to wash up alone too.

349
00:30:17,565 --> 00:30:19,567
Even so, you shouldn't be the one
washing me.

350
00:30:24,322 --> 00:30:26,574
- Go now before it gets more awkward.
- Okay.

351
00:30:27,075 --> 00:30:27,909
Okay, then.

352
00:30:28,493 --> 00:30:31,036
Call me if you need anything urgently.

353
00:30:31,037 --> 00:30:32,789
I'll always be one step behind you.

354
00:30:33,957 --> 00:30:34,791
Okay.

355
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:37,377
Okay, good.

356
00:30:40,004 --> 00:30:40,921
Gang-rok.

357
00:30:40,922 --> 00:30:43,049
Yes? Yes, sir.

358
00:30:45,677 --> 00:30:47,053
You should be careful.

359
00:30:49,764 --> 00:30:54,351
Baek Sang-gil knows that you're here
and that you helped me.

360
00:30:54,352 --> 00:30:57,438
Well, why would he care about
someone like me?

361
00:30:58,189 --> 00:30:59,190
Don't worry.

362
00:30:59,816 --> 00:31:03,361
I might not be as good as you,
but I'm still a pretty good fight…

363
00:31:06,948 --> 00:31:09,242
Who are you? Who do you work for, damn it!

364
00:31:09,742 --> 00:31:11,953
Sir, I've still got it.

365
00:31:12,745 --> 00:31:13,705
Don't worry.

366
00:31:14,205 --> 00:31:15,290
Please rest.

367
00:31:20,295 --> 00:31:22,964
Sir, if anything happens,
please contact me immediately.

368
00:32:01,628 --> 00:32:02,629
Good morning.

369
00:32:57,308 --> 00:32:59,686
She must have arrived safely, right?

370
00:33:00,603 --> 00:33:03,272
I wonder if she'll find some comfort
in living there.

371
00:33:04,232 --> 00:33:06,817
This place is so beautiful.

372
00:33:06,818 --> 00:33:10,154
I bet living somewhere like this
would feel like a dream.

373
00:33:20,081 --> 00:33:22,208
I hope she's not having too hard a time.

374
00:33:23,835 --> 00:33:24,836
Go Eun-sae.

375
00:33:26,170 --> 00:33:27,880
That's not her name.

376
00:33:33,469 --> 00:33:34,679
Her name is Blessing.

377
00:33:35,304 --> 00:33:38,056
I chose it as it's a blessing
for her to have settled here.

378
00:33:38,057 --> 00:33:39,058
What…

379
00:33:39,809 --> 00:33:40,643
What happened?

380
00:33:41,602 --> 00:33:42,478
Why are you here?

381
00:33:45,356 --> 00:33:46,398
"What happened?"

382
00:33:46,399 --> 00:33:50,028
After doing something so huge to me,
how can you ask what happened?

383
00:33:51,112 --> 00:33:53,156
I was so scared, I could've died.

384
00:33:54,866 --> 00:33:56,492
Man, this is crazy.

385
00:33:57,410 --> 00:33:59,327
Why didn't you go to Japan?

386
00:33:59,328 --> 00:34:00,538
Why would I go to Japan?

387
00:34:01,122 --> 00:34:04,458
Stowaway? Why would I have to stow away?
I didn't do anything wrong.

388
00:34:04,459 --> 00:34:06,460
Because you'd be safe that way.

389
00:34:06,461 --> 00:34:08,503
I can be safe without going.

390
00:34:08,504 --> 00:34:09,630
I can just

391
00:34:10,965 --> 00:34:12,175
break up with Jang Tae-ha.

392
00:34:15,303 --> 00:34:17,262
- What?
- Why are you so surprised?

393
00:34:17,263 --> 00:34:19,681
You knew I hated gangsters.
If you were going back,

394
00:34:19,682 --> 00:34:21,350
you should've prepared to lose me.

395
00:34:25,605 --> 00:34:29,442
The reason you sent me away was
that you went back to being a gangster.

396
00:34:31,277 --> 00:34:35,406
So if I ended things with you,
wouldn't I be safe?

397
00:34:38,618 --> 00:34:41,578
Even if that's true,
you have nowhere to go right now.

398
00:34:41,579 --> 00:34:42,788
I'll go to a facility.

399
00:34:42,789 --> 00:34:46,125
And we're strangers now,
so don't ask me any more questions.

400
00:34:55,593 --> 00:34:56,469
Did…

401
00:34:58,596 --> 00:35:00,515
some of your memory

402
00:35:01,140 --> 00:35:02,433
come back?

403
00:35:04,477 --> 00:35:07,480
No. What, I can't break up with you
if my memory hasn't returned?

404
00:35:09,065 --> 00:35:11,858
I came here to say we're breaking up,
and I'll be fine.

405
00:35:11,859 --> 00:35:15,238
Thanks for taking care of me until now.
I'll just take my things and leave.

406
00:35:26,749 --> 00:35:27,959
What…

407
00:35:29,293 --> 00:35:30,753
Wait, what…

408
00:35:32,380 --> 00:35:35,258
Where are all my things?

409
00:35:36,217 --> 00:35:38,552
I sent everything to Japan yesterday.

410
00:35:38,553 --> 00:35:39,594
What?

411
00:35:39,595 --> 00:35:43,348
I asked Mr. Hong to send your things
after we left.

412
00:35:43,349 --> 00:35:45,935
But why… How could you…

413
00:35:47,728 --> 00:35:49,855
Call and ask them to send it back
right away.

414
00:35:49,856 --> 00:35:52,065
Something important is in there.

415
00:35:52,066 --> 00:35:53,400
- Hurry.
- Okay.

416
00:35:53,401 --> 00:35:54,318
Hurry.

417
00:35:58,447 --> 00:35:59,614
What did they say?

418
00:35:59,615 --> 00:36:03,201
If they send it back right away,
it should arrive by tomorrow afternoon.

419
00:36:03,202 --> 00:36:04,162
Tomorrow afternoon?

420
00:36:05,246 --> 00:36:06,664
What do I do?

421
00:36:14,297 --> 00:36:16,883
I guess I have no choice but to

422
00:36:17,466 --> 00:36:18,634
stay here tonight.

423
00:36:21,220 --> 00:36:23,763
The package won't get here until tomorrow.

424
00:36:23,764 --> 00:36:27,184
It'd be impractical to go to Seoul today
and come back tomorrow.

425
00:36:27,185 --> 00:36:30,354
You must've already said you want
to break up. How tragically funny.

426
00:36:31,939 --> 00:36:32,981
Yeah, I know.

427
00:36:32,982 --> 00:36:34,650
Well, I guess you have no choice.

428
00:36:35,234 --> 00:36:36,861
Enjoy the sleepover.

429
00:36:39,113 --> 00:36:41,616
<i>I'm with Go Eun-sae now.
Call me when you see this.</i>

430
00:36:50,666 --> 00:36:52,501
Don't you dare try to ship me off again.

431
00:36:53,377 --> 00:36:57,173
I'm not someone who obediently goes
wherever you tell me to go.

432
00:36:59,425 --> 00:37:01,135
You were never particularly

433
00:37:01,802 --> 00:37:02,637
obedient.

434
00:37:08,643 --> 00:37:11,646
It seems like you really let yourself go
while I was gone.

435
00:37:12,521 --> 00:37:13,522
What?

436
00:37:18,903 --> 00:37:20,196
I just left the hospital.

437
00:37:25,534 --> 00:37:27,036
I can't believe you.

438
00:37:32,333 --> 00:37:34,877
What are you doing? Go take a shower.

439
00:37:37,171 --> 00:37:39,172
- Are you okay?
- Yeah.

440
00:37:39,173 --> 00:37:40,465
I'm sorry.

441
00:37:40,466 --> 00:37:42,593
You're more hurt than I thought.

442
00:37:45,179 --> 00:37:46,013
Then

443
00:37:46,764 --> 00:37:48,933
you mustn't be able to shower on your own.

444
00:37:52,937 --> 00:37:53,771
Right?

445
00:38:00,403 --> 00:38:01,570
There's nothing to wash.

446
00:38:02,905 --> 00:38:04,240
But I have a lot of hair.

447
00:38:04,991 --> 00:38:06,617
I meant that you have a small head.

448
00:38:14,041 --> 00:38:16,376
I can dry it myself.

449
00:38:16,377 --> 00:38:17,878
Just stay put.

450
00:38:31,100 --> 00:38:33,853
<i>I can just break up with Jang Tae-ha.</i>

451
00:38:38,357 --> 00:38:40,401
Now you look better.

452
00:38:42,111 --> 00:38:44,404
Was I that hideous to look at?

453
00:38:44,405 --> 00:38:45,448
Yes.

454
00:38:54,665 --> 00:38:57,918
- Which facility are you going to?
- I told you not to ask.

455
00:38:58,419 --> 00:38:59,545
I told you, we broke up.

456
00:39:00,838 --> 00:39:02,047
We can still stay in--

457
00:39:02,048 --> 00:39:03,632
You've never washed her, right?

458
00:39:04,216 --> 00:39:05,051
What?

459
00:39:07,094 --> 00:39:07,928
No.

460
00:39:09,055 --> 00:39:10,306
I knew it.

461
00:39:10,890 --> 00:39:14,810
Everyone in this house ends up so dirty
if I'm not around.

462
00:39:16,812 --> 00:39:18,147
Come on, follow me.

463
00:39:25,071 --> 00:39:27,281
I wonder if she'll turn into a white dog.

464
00:39:36,082 --> 00:39:37,457
- My eyes.
- It's in your eyes?

465
00:39:37,458 --> 00:39:38,918
- The soap…
- Are you okay?

466
00:40:04,402 --> 00:40:05,444
Are you okay?

467
00:40:12,201 --> 00:40:13,035
Ma'am!

468
00:40:14,703 --> 00:40:18,039
We stopped by
because we heard you were here.

469
00:40:18,040 --> 00:40:21,460
Yeah, so we came in a hurry.

470
00:40:22,002 --> 00:40:24,712
But… should we come back later?

471
00:40:24,713 --> 00:40:25,630
No…

472
00:40:25,631 --> 00:40:27,800
Are you feeling okay, Eun-sae?

473
00:40:28,300 --> 00:40:32,012
You all knew I was going far away,
but you kept it from me.

474
00:40:33,055 --> 00:40:35,640
But what happened?

475
00:40:35,641 --> 00:40:37,434
Where were you all this time?

476
00:40:37,435 --> 00:40:39,562
Jang Tae-ha can fill you in.

477
00:40:41,105 --> 00:40:42,189
Where are you going?

478
00:40:43,232 --> 00:40:45,400
I'm going to get something for our dinner.

479
00:40:45,401 --> 00:40:48,279
Don't follow me, Jang Tae-ha.
Explain to them what's going on.

480
00:40:49,071 --> 00:40:50,489
And catch Blessing and bathe her.

481
00:40:55,911 --> 00:40:57,120
Hey, what the heck?

482
00:40:57,121 --> 00:40:59,540
Why is she suddenly so cold to you?

483
00:41:03,210 --> 00:41:04,044
What happened?

484
00:41:06,755 --> 00:41:09,258
You should have told me
if you knew she hadn't gone.

485
00:41:09,758 --> 00:41:11,343
That was because

486
00:41:11,927 --> 00:41:16,222
we knew you'd go looking for her
even though you were in no state to.

487
00:41:16,223 --> 00:41:21,228
But I'm really glad
Eun-sae showed up safe and sound.

488
00:41:22,396 --> 00:41:28,277
But she can't stay in Taffy Village
anymore, right?

489
00:41:29,653 --> 00:41:33,948
Since Baek Sang-gil knows about it,
it's not as safe as it used to be.

490
00:41:33,949 --> 00:41:36,910
I asked Kaito to find out
when the next stowaway boat will leave,

491
00:41:36,911 --> 00:41:38,703
but it'll take a while.

492
00:41:38,704 --> 00:41:40,706
And it won't be easy
to convince Go Eun-sae.

493
00:41:41,665 --> 00:41:42,874
On that note,

494
00:41:42,875 --> 00:41:46,504
did you happen to see an odd suit
and sneakers when you packed her stuff?

495
00:41:47,922 --> 00:41:49,714
- Did you see them?
- No.

496
00:41:49,715 --> 00:41:50,965
Did you see them?

497
00:41:50,966 --> 00:41:52,426
Odd?

498
00:41:52,927 --> 00:41:55,553
I think the plan B evidence
Baek Sang-gil is looking for

499
00:41:55,554 --> 00:41:58,806
is in the outfit Go Eun-sae was wearing
at the time of the incident.

500
00:41:58,807 --> 00:42:03,186
Somewhere like the buttons on the suit,
the belt, or the sneakers.

501
00:42:03,187 --> 00:42:04,813
That makes sense.

502
00:42:06,273 --> 00:42:09,193
We'll have to look for that first
when her stuff comes back.

503
00:42:09,944 --> 00:42:11,653
If we find that evidence,

504
00:42:11,654 --> 00:42:13,614
we may be able to keep her safe

505
00:42:14,782 --> 00:42:16,283
without having to send her away.

506
00:42:21,163 --> 00:42:24,875
LETTER OF RESIGNATION
NAME: MIN SU-JI

507
00:42:27,962 --> 00:42:30,381
Maybe hating me
will make it hurt a little less.

508
00:42:47,189 --> 00:42:48,398
What are you doing?

509
00:42:48,399 --> 00:42:50,733
You asked to see me,
and now you've gone quiet?

510
00:42:50,734 --> 00:42:51,610
What?

511
00:42:52,778 --> 00:42:53,904
Right, I…

512
00:42:55,990 --> 00:42:59,368
I… realized something recently.

513
00:43:00,119 --> 00:43:02,830
I'd been standing in a field of flowers.

514
00:43:03,539 --> 00:43:06,417
Some people are forced to break up
even when they love someone

515
00:43:07,585 --> 00:43:09,044
enough to risk their lives.

516
00:43:10,504 --> 00:43:14,717
Even fighting over our pride like this
feels like a luxury.

517
00:43:15,467 --> 00:43:16,302
I wanted to say…

518
00:43:20,264 --> 00:43:21,473
I'm sorry for everything.

519
00:43:23,100 --> 00:43:25,351
For the times I didn't mean to,

520
00:43:25,352 --> 00:43:30,232
and the times I did mean to hurt you
the way I did.

521
00:43:30,733 --> 00:43:31,859
I'm sorry for everything.

522
00:43:33,777 --> 00:43:34,612
And…

523
00:43:36,822 --> 00:43:38,824
I really liked you a lot, Min Su-ji.

524
00:43:40,701 --> 00:43:43,620
I actually don't really like <i>yulmu</i> tea.

525
00:43:43,621 --> 00:43:46,247
But when I ordered it,

526
00:43:46,248 --> 00:43:50,753
I was able to see you some more,
so I ordered several cups.

527
00:43:55,424 --> 00:43:56,467
Here's your <i>yulmu</i> tea.

528
00:43:57,718 --> 00:43:58,552
Thanks.

529
00:43:59,053 --> 00:44:01,221
I just love <i>yulmu</i> tea.

530
00:44:08,687 --> 00:44:10,939
When I dated you,
someone who I liked so much,

531
00:44:11,440 --> 00:44:12,316
I really felt like

532
00:44:13,192 --> 00:44:14,943
I had the whole world.

533
00:44:16,487 --> 00:44:19,073
But people are so fickle and petty.

534
00:44:19,907 --> 00:44:21,241
I forgot all about that.

535
00:44:23,494 --> 00:44:24,453
So now I'll

536
00:44:25,746 --> 00:44:26,747
respect your decision.

537
00:44:27,873 --> 00:44:29,958
You can stop coming to the clinic.

538
00:44:32,252 --> 00:44:33,544
An Gi-jun…

539
00:44:33,545 --> 00:44:36,256
And, as you wanted,

540
00:44:37,257 --> 00:44:40,386
let's break up now.

541
00:44:47,726 --> 00:44:49,853
I'll get going, then.

542
00:45:06,245 --> 00:45:10,040
This isn't really
your type of cuisine, is it?

543
00:45:10,958 --> 00:45:13,376
I guess my taste buds changed
after I almost died.

544
00:45:13,377 --> 00:45:14,627
Everyone, dig in.

545
00:45:14,628 --> 00:45:17,255
- Okay.
- Thank you for the food.

546
00:45:17,256 --> 00:45:19,924
- I don't know what to start with.
- This looks good.

547
00:45:19,925 --> 00:45:23,137
- I've never tried this.
- I can't even make this.

548
00:45:25,597 --> 00:45:27,141
You're in your twenties, Gang-rok.

549
00:45:27,725 --> 00:45:31,895
They say black chicken legs are good
for people in their thirties and older.

550
00:45:32,563 --> 00:45:34,689
I guess that means I qualify.

551
00:45:34,690 --> 00:45:36,441
Yeah, you do.

552
00:45:36,442 --> 00:45:37,359
Abalone.

553
00:45:42,448 --> 00:45:43,991
The abalone smells a bit fishy.

554
00:45:44,908 --> 00:45:47,161
You should eat this, Jang Tae-ha.

555
00:45:50,664 --> 00:45:52,624
You should eat some too.

556
00:45:53,208 --> 00:45:54,584
Yeah, thanks.

557
00:45:54,585 --> 00:45:56,545
I can eat the chicken neck, right?

558
00:45:57,504 --> 00:45:58,797
Eat some shrimp too.

559
00:45:59,506 --> 00:46:01,132
Long time no see, shrimp.

560
00:46:01,133 --> 00:46:03,676
There's a lot of kimchi. Eat up.

561
00:46:03,677 --> 00:46:05,971
Wow, so much kimchi.

562
00:46:11,310 --> 00:46:12,811
I ate, but I'm still hungry.

563
00:46:19,193 --> 00:46:23,529
Didn't it seem like the menu was
for Tae-ha's health and recovery?

564
00:46:23,530 --> 00:46:24,364
Yeah.

565
00:46:24,865 --> 00:46:27,074
And if they're about to break up,

566
00:46:27,075 --> 00:46:29,745
isn't it weird that she said
she'd sleep over?

567
00:46:30,621 --> 00:46:31,621
She has our place.

568
00:46:31,622 --> 00:46:33,665
And the S.E.S ladies' places too.

569
00:46:34,166 --> 00:46:35,666
She didn't have to…

570
00:46:35,667 --> 00:46:36,877
That's what I'm saying.

571
00:46:38,212 --> 00:46:39,046
What's going on?

572
00:46:39,797 --> 00:46:42,507
Seemingly distant, but still close…

573
00:46:42,508 --> 00:46:44,676
This sticky feeling.

574
00:46:49,556 --> 00:46:50,891
Take that off now.

575
00:46:56,104 --> 00:46:57,021
Do what?

576
00:46:57,022 --> 00:46:59,273
We have to disinfect the wound.

577
00:46:59,274 --> 00:47:01,276
Mr. Hong said to make sure to do it.

578
00:47:06,406 --> 00:47:07,241
Right.

579
00:47:07,741 --> 00:47:09,535
I can do this myself.

580
00:47:10,744 --> 00:47:13,287
Is your arm two meters long or something?

581
00:47:13,288 --> 00:47:15,540
How will you disinfect
a wound on your back?

582
00:47:15,541 --> 00:47:16,999
Really, it's okay.

583
00:47:17,000 --> 00:47:19,044
Hurry up.

584
00:47:39,815 --> 00:47:41,483
You said you were a good fighter.

585
00:47:42,192 --> 00:47:43,234
That was a total lie.

586
00:47:43,235 --> 00:47:45,362
You got hurt badly.

587
00:47:47,030 --> 00:47:50,909
I guess you were so shocked
that you didn't see it properly.

588
00:47:51,827 --> 00:47:53,828
I took on almost 20 guys from the start.

589
00:47:53,829 --> 00:47:55,080
Zip it.

590
00:48:08,886 --> 00:48:11,013
Anyway, thank you for saving me.

591
00:48:12,431 --> 00:48:17,519
Even if we're breaking up,
I'm still grateful.

592
00:48:25,193 --> 00:48:27,321
While I was living with you…

593
00:48:29,364 --> 00:48:31,241
I felt so secure.

594
00:48:33,285 --> 00:48:37,205
No matter how dangerous things got,
I wasn't afraid.

595
00:48:39,541 --> 00:48:44,463
Even the world's tallest mountain
wouldn't have stood taller than your back.

596
00:48:52,888 --> 00:48:55,140
Thank you so much

597
00:48:56,892 --> 00:48:58,685
for risking your life to save me.

598
00:49:27,714 --> 00:49:29,424
Just wait a little bit.

599
00:49:30,676 --> 00:49:33,095
I'll protect you now.

600
00:49:44,189 --> 00:49:45,565
I promise I will.

601
00:50:27,816 --> 00:50:29,692
- Touch.
- Keep your guard up.

602
00:50:29,693 --> 00:50:31,152
37 YEARS AGO

603
00:50:31,153 --> 00:50:32,320
Move back.

604
00:50:33,905 --> 00:50:35,197
Keep your guard up.

605
00:50:35,198 --> 00:50:36,199
Hello, sir!

606
00:50:37,200 --> 00:50:39,161
Nice to meet you. I'm Hong Do-yeop.

607
00:50:41,163 --> 00:50:42,706
I'm Baek Sang-gil. I just joined.

608
00:50:43,206 --> 00:50:45,500
I've been a fan since the Asian Games.

609
00:50:46,001 --> 00:50:47,502
You're my role model.

610
00:50:48,670 --> 00:50:49,546
I see.

611
00:51:11,234 --> 00:51:12,360
<i>You lost.</i>

612
00:51:38,136 --> 00:51:40,430
Has it been about 30 years or so?

613
00:51:40,931 --> 00:51:44,518
I think you had about a dozen bottles here
back then too.

614
00:51:46,186 --> 00:51:47,813
You have a good memory.

615
00:51:52,776 --> 00:51:54,152
Back then, I…

616
00:51:56,279 --> 00:51:57,614
really felt like shit.

617
00:52:00,700 --> 00:52:03,703
I thought drinking hard liquor
would help me feel better.

618
00:52:07,207 --> 00:52:08,083
What is it?

619
00:52:09,417 --> 00:52:11,628
Angry about something today too?
Like back then?

620
00:52:16,091 --> 00:52:16,925
Angry?

621
00:52:18,718 --> 00:52:21,012
It's not anger. What should I call it?

622
00:52:22,556 --> 00:52:24,266
It feels filthier than that.

623
00:52:31,523 --> 00:52:33,066
A filthy sense of defeat.

624
00:52:35,152 --> 00:52:38,530
It's been a long time
since I felt this filthy feeling.

625
00:52:42,284 --> 00:52:44,995
Back then, I didn't know what to do
about this feeling.

626
00:52:48,081 --> 00:52:49,082
I think I know now.

627
00:52:54,129 --> 00:52:56,006
One thing can cover up a sense of defeat.

628
00:52:58,800 --> 00:52:59,718
Winning.

629
00:53:04,389 --> 00:53:05,557
This time…

630
00:53:10,520 --> 00:53:12,105
I must win no matter what.

631
00:53:27,913 --> 00:53:30,540
RETURNED

632
00:53:39,007 --> 00:53:40,341
Look.

633
00:53:40,342 --> 00:53:43,678
I have a lot of underwear in here.
Can you leave?

634
00:53:44,721 --> 00:53:46,014
Right, sure.

635
00:54:21,716 --> 00:54:23,218
I found it.

636
00:54:24,928 --> 00:54:28,305
When you get there,
please let me know her destination.

637
00:54:28,306 --> 00:54:30,766
Goodness, if you're so worried,

638
00:54:30,767 --> 00:54:32,810
why don't you take her there yourself?

639
00:54:32,811 --> 00:54:35,396
I want to, but she insists
she doesn't want me to.

640
00:54:35,397 --> 00:54:37,732
- Okay.
- Thank you.

641
00:54:46,324 --> 00:54:47,492
I'll get going now.

642
00:54:53,164 --> 00:54:54,916
Take care of yourself.

643
00:54:56,376 --> 00:54:57,377
Go Eun-sae.

644
00:55:00,630 --> 00:55:02,424
Even though you said we're breaking up…

645
00:55:04,551 --> 00:55:05,635
I still like you.

646
00:55:08,805 --> 00:55:10,098
So if you're ever in danger

647
00:55:10,682 --> 00:55:11,599
or scared,

648
00:55:13,268 --> 00:55:14,436
or if anything happens…

649
00:55:17,063 --> 00:55:18,565
If you need help,

650
00:55:19,774 --> 00:55:21,442
feel free to call me anytime.

651
00:55:21,443 --> 00:55:22,527
It's okay to do that.

652
00:55:32,120 --> 00:55:33,830
I will call when I get there.

653
00:55:35,999 --> 00:55:38,918
But not you. I'll call Jeong-hwa.

654
00:56:04,194 --> 00:56:06,446
Jang Tae-ha, you seriously…

655
00:56:12,535 --> 00:56:15,497
She never took out that suit
or the sneakers while she was here.

656
00:56:16,623 --> 00:56:18,208
But she decided to take them?

657
00:56:19,751 --> 00:56:21,835
<i>Call and ask them to send it back
right away.</i>

658
00:56:21,836 --> 00:56:23,380
Something important is in there.

659
00:56:29,177 --> 00:56:30,220
HONG DO-YEOP

660
00:56:30,929 --> 00:56:31,845
Yes?

661
00:56:31,846 --> 00:56:34,264
Are you with Gang-rok by any chance?

662
00:56:34,265 --> 00:56:35,474
<i>I'm not. Why?</i>

663
00:56:35,475 --> 00:56:40,270
I wanted to eat with him, but I haven't
been able to reach him for a while.

664
00:56:40,271 --> 00:56:41,814
I'll go to his place.

665
00:56:41,815 --> 00:56:43,108
<i>Okay, do that.</i>

666
00:56:43,983 --> 00:56:45,402
Gang-rok!

667
00:56:47,654 --> 00:56:48,822
Kim Gang-rok.

668
00:56:52,909 --> 00:56:54,369
Where did he go?

669
00:57:06,131 --> 00:57:08,549
<i>Baek Sang-gil knows that you're here</i>

670
00:57:08,550 --> 00:57:10,343
and that you helped me.

671
00:57:11,010 --> 00:57:12,345
You should be careful.

672
00:57:23,022 --> 00:57:25,650
KIM GANG-ROK
MY CURRENT LOCATION

673
00:57:48,590 --> 00:57:49,966
Hey, watch out!

674
00:57:56,181 --> 00:57:57,474
Is this bastard crazy?

675
00:58:03,271 --> 00:58:05,231
Hey, you bastard!

676
00:58:13,031 --> 00:58:14,616
You son of a bitch!

677
00:58:17,410 --> 00:58:19,621
Gang-rok, stay with me.

678
00:58:20,205 --> 00:58:21,247
Gang-rok!

679
00:58:24,250 --> 00:58:26,544
I told you I'm a good fighter.

680
00:58:27,587 --> 00:58:28,713
Why did you come here?

681
00:58:43,394 --> 00:58:44,229
Hold on to me.

682
00:59:00,787 --> 00:59:01,745
Hang in there.

683
00:59:01,746 --> 00:59:03,456
Just until we get to the hospital.

684
01:02:01,175 --> 01:02:03,344
Jeong-hwa!

685
01:02:04,011 --> 01:02:05,012
Jeong-hwa!

686
01:02:05,888 --> 01:02:07,264
Jeong-hwa!

687
01:02:07,265 --> 01:02:09,934
Damn it! Jeong-hwa!

688
01:02:21,362 --> 01:02:22,488
Jeong-hwa!

689
01:02:29,245 --> 01:02:30,163
Jeong-hwa!

690
01:02:56,063 --> 01:02:58,149
My Jeong-hwa.

691
01:03:10,912 --> 01:03:12,580
OUR STICKY LOVE

692
01:03:59,210 --> 01:04:03,172
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
